node_modules/
# wrangler's local state (the build renders through the app's worker in Miniflare)
.wrangler/
# The worker's own output: the client bundle and the worker the build emits beside `dist/app`.
# Only `dist/app` — the artifact view and the assets — is embedded, and only it is tracked.
dist/client/
dist/server/

# `dist/app/` IS TRACKED — deliberately, and it is not build noise here.
#
# `src/panel.rs` embeds the whole directory with `include_dir!`, which reads it at COMPILE time,
# and fabric code-splits: the entry does `import("./sdfEngine-<hash>.js")`, which reaches
# `sdf.wgsl` in turn, and the custom protocol serves those out of the embedded copy. So a clone
# without `dist/` does not "just miss an optimisation" — it fails to build, or builds a panel that
# 404s every lazy chunk at runtime. The files under `assets/` are written compressed by the
# build (`native({ compress })` — `*.gz` or `*.br`, the suffix names the decoder) and decoded by
# the protocol handler — so they are binary blobs here, and a diff of them means nothing.
#
# The hashed filenames change on every build, so this directory churns. That is the price of
# `include_dir!`; the alternative is a build.rs that runs vite, which would make `cargo build`
# depend on node.
# the ambient types the build writes
.phaze/
# the web plugin's build sentinel
dist/.build-complete
